e_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-29T16:09:19Z","updated_at":"2024-05-29T16:09:19Z","body":"> Alright, 2.32.3 is out. Thanks everyone for your patience, please let us know if you're still hitting this failure case after upgrading.\r\n\r\nWith 2.32.0-2.32.2 I've been seeing the same issue when using requests_pkcs12; now with 2.32.3, the issue did unfortunately not disappear but rather move to `HTTPSConnectionPool(host='some.system', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: /foo/bar (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: unable to get local issuer certificate (_ssl.c:1006)')))`.\r\n\r\nI've opened an issue with requests_pkcs12, but since you specifically asked to point out problems where things do not behave like in 2.31.0...","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2137782363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2139110295","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6715#issuecomment-2139110295","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/6715","id":2139110295,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs5_gDuX","user":{"login":"Heraldk","id":1530351,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzAzNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1530351?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk","html_url":"https://github.com/Heraldk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Heraldk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-30T09:10:36Z","updated_at":"2024-05-30T09:10:36Z","body":"We also use requests_pkcs12 and I can confirm that 2.32.3 doesn't work with it. Stack trace I saw:\r\n\r\n`\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/workspace/.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 715, in urlopen\r\n    httplib_response = self._make_request(\r\n                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/workspace/.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 404, in _make_request\r\n    self._validate_conn(conn)\r\n  File \"/workspace/.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py\", line 1058, in _validate_conn\r\n    conn.connect()\r\n  File \"/workspace/.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/urllib3/connection.py\", line 419, in connect\r\n    self.sock = ssl_wrap_socket(\r\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/workspace/.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/urllib3/util/ssl_.py\", line 449, in ssl_wrap_socket\r\n    ssl_sock = _ssl_wrap_socket_impl(\r\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/workspace/.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/urllib3/util/ssl_.py\", line 493, in _ssl_wrap_socket_impl\r\n    return ssl_context.wrap_socket(sock, server_hostname=server_hostname)\r\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.11/ssl.py\", line 517, in wrap_socket\r\n    return self.sslsocket_class._create(\r\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.11/ssl.py\", line 1108, in _create\r\n    self.do_handshake()\r\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.11/ssl.py\", line 1379, in do_handshake\r\n    self._sslobj.do_handshake()\r\nssl.SSLCertVerificationError: [SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: unable to get local issuer certificate (_ssl.c:1006)\r\n`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2139110295/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2481193018","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6715#issuecomment-2481193018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/6715","id":2481193018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs6T5AA6","user":{"login":"suaveolent","id":2163625,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjM2MjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2163625?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent","html_url":"https://github.com/suaveolent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suaveolent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-17T11:26:31Z","updated_at":"2024-11-17T11:26:31Z","body":"I am seeing a similar behaviour with `2.32.3` and `build_connection_pool_key_attributes`with a self-signed certificate.\r\nI need a custom ssl context since otherwise the connection will faile due to weak certificate strength.\r\n\r\n\r\nHere is my code:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport ssl\r\nimport requests\r\nfrom requests.adapters import HTTPAdapter\r\n\r\n\r\nclass SSLAdapter(HTTPAdapter):\r\n    \"\"\"An HTTPAdapter that uses an arbitrary SSL context.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, ssl_context: ssl.SSLContext = None, **kwargs):\r\n        \"\"\"Initialize the SSLAdapter.\"\"\"\r\n        super().__init__(**kwargs)\r\n        self.ssl_context = ssl_context\r\n\r\n    def build_connection_pool_key_attributes(\r\n        self,\r\n        request: requests.PreparedRequest,\r\n        verify: bool | str,\r\n        cert: str | tuple[str, str] | None = None,\r\n    ) -> tuple[dict, dict]:\r\n        host_params, ssl_params = super().build_connection_pool_key_attributes(\r\n            request, verify, cert\r\n        )\r\n        if verify is True and self.ssl_context:\r\n            ssl_params[\"ssl_context\"] = self.ssl_context\r\n\r\n        return host_params, ssl_params\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    # Create a custom SSL context\r\n    ssl_context = ssl._create_unverified_context()\r\n    ssl_context.set_ciphers(\"DEFAULT@SECLEVEL=2\")  # Adjusting the security level to support 2048 bit keys\r\n\r\n    # Example API call setup\r\n    username = \"<admin>\"\r\n    password = \"<password>\"\r\n    protocol = \"https\"\r\n    api_url = f\"{protocol}://<host>/\"\r\n    action = \"<action>\"\r\n    headers = {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\r\n\r\n    # Create a session with the SSLAdapter\r\n    session = requests.Session()\r\n    session.auth = (username, password)\r\n    session.mount(f\"{protocol}://\", SSLAdapter(ssl_context = ssl_context))\r\n\r\n    try:\r\n        response = session.get(api_url + action, timeout=15, headers=headers)\r\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an exception for HTTP errors\r\n        print(\"Response:\", response.json())\r\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\r\n        print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich results in this error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nAn error occurred: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='<host>', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: /<action>/ (Caused by SSLError(SSLCertVerificationError(1, '[SSL: CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED] certificate verify failed: self-signed certificate (_ssl.c:1000)')))\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat am I doing wrong? Shouldn't `_create_unverified_context` exacly allow for self-signed certs? ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2481193018/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2560741069","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6715#issuecomment-2560741069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/6715","id":2560741069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs6Yoc7N","user":{"login":"CraftedCat","id":38719532,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NzE5NTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38719532?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat","html_url":"https://github.com/CraftedCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CraftedCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-24T06:54:09Z","updated_at":"2024-12-24T06: